**Plan: parse the flag in `cli.js`, print `buildRows()` as JSON.** No change to `report.js` or `format.js`.

```js
function main(argv) {
  const args = argv.filter((a) => a !== '--json');
  if (args[0] !== 'report') { process.stderr.write(USAGE + '\n'); return 1; }
  const rows = buildRows();
  const out = argv.includes('--json') ? JSON.stringify(rows, null, 2) : toTable(rows);
  process.stdout.write(out + '\n');
  return 0;
}
```

One call to make. The table drops `owner` and `slow` on purpose, per [format.js:3](src/format.js:3). I would emit the full row, since JSON has no width limit. Say the word if you want the four table columns only.
